Z||000000||fastback87||11-18-2001||03:51 PM||||what are the differences between the flywheels on the duke and the 2.8?  Are they the same?  I am wanting to put a v6 or a V8 in a 2m4 and would like to know if I can use the dukes flywheel?  Anybody know?  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||ray b||11-18-2001||04:47 PM||||NO use the flywheel for the v6 and besure it is the correct year for the motor.<BR>88 is different from early v6, 3.1 and 3.4 used the 88 flywheel.<BR>v8 needs its own flywheel.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||13
Z||000002||fastback87||11-18-2001||04:54 PM||||how does the V8 flywheel fit in the th125 bell housing.||||reg||5
Z||000003||jelly2m8||11-18-2001||07:03 PM||||The V8 flexplate will not fit in the auto's bell housing. Way too big.<P> The 4 banger and the V6 use a different bolt pattern, so you won't be able to physically mix them between the 2 engines. The SBC uses a different pattren also. <P> The 4 banger and the 88 V6 flywheel are neutrally balanced.<P>The 85-87 V6 flywheels are balanced.<P>A flywheel is used on a manual tranny car, a flex plate is used in automatic cars.<P><BR> If you go V8, use one of Archies kits. He will supply either the correct flywheel for your application, or the correct flex plate adaptor for your current flexplate.<p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 11-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||fastback87||11-22-2001||12:26 AM||||Does archie make his own flywheel, NOT FLEXPLATE, or does he use one that already exists?  I am trying to build a V8 fiero Manual tranny, and need to know if I have to use archie's kit or if a flywheel exists by itself?||||reg||1
Z||000005||jelly2m8||11-22-2001||12:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fastback87:<BR><B>Does archie make his own flywheel, NOT FLEXPLATE, or does he use one that already exists?  I am trying to build a V8 fiero Manual tranny, and need to know if I have to use archie's kit or if a flywheel exists by itself?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I THINK  that Archie has the flywheels specially manufactured for his kits.<P> E-mail him, I'm sure he'll reply<P> I bought a used incomplete automatic kit, and used the 4 banger flywheel on Archies flex plate adaptor, so I can't tell you if there is any numbers on it.<P>Either way, deal with Archie, he'll hook you up.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
